Subject: [PATCH] KrissOS round title bar buttons, on either side

The server-side title bar draws its own minimize, maximize and close:
a soft circle in a 46 x 32 px target (Windows 11's caption button
width), tinted with the accent under the pointer and pressed, with close
turning red. Glyphs are thin rounded SVGs recoloured from the theme, so
they read on light and dark, and dim on an unfocused window. A button
acts on release over the button it was pressed on.

Side and order come from `window_buttons` in com.system76.CosmicTk, in
GNOME's button-layout form (":minimize,maximize,close" on the right,
"close,minimize,maximize:" on the left), and change live. Hovering
maximize now tells kriss_snap_v1 from the button itself instead of
from a fixed offset from the right edge, so snap layouts work on
either side.
---
